  6	 * Theme-free card renderers shared by RPC hosts (keating tui, e2e tests).
  7	 * The classic Pi shell keeps its themed equivalents in
  8	 * src/pi/hyper-teacher/tui-components.ts; these emit plain strings so they
  9	 * survive JSON transport and render in any terminal without pi-tui.
 10	 *
 11	 * Tool results that cross the RPC boundary are JSON-serialized, so Maps
 12	 * (e.g. quiz.answerKey) arrive as plain objects or empty objects — every
 13	 * accessor here tolerates both.
